  "notes": [
    "Koninginneweg 1 / Van Eeghenstraat 222-230 (pand 0363100012236925, built 1905, 366 LoD2.2 wall surfaces from the PDOK 3D Basisvoorziening tile because the 3DBAG API timed out; roof max 26.2 m): a five-storey apartment villa block on the Vondelpark's south edge, pink-red brick with cream speklagen, a grey stone souterrain, segmental window heads in cream voussoirs with keystones, iron balconets, a slate mansard with pedimented dormers, and white timber verandas.",
    "walls[0] park front (surfaces of panels 155, 289, 118; crop w01-341p 2021-03-26 from the park path, 47 m, winter): three storeys of tall white-framed windows in ten columns over a light raised ground storey, cream bands at sill and head lines, a cornice, an attic row of wide windows; foliage 22 % of the crop.",
    "walls[1] Koninginneweg front (panels 6, 45, 131, 216; crop w02-245w 2022-03-22): grey stone souterrain, three window storeys with segmental heads, cream voussoirs and keystones, speklagen every half metre, iron balconets; in the middle a stone arcade of two round arches with a balustrade on the ground storey and a white timber loggia of two round arches on the first floor with an iron railing on its roof deck (new `gallery` component); mansard with three pedimented dormers.",
    "walls[2] south fronts on the west block (panels 185, 98; crops w03-155w 2019-01-17, w04-156w 2022-03-22): the same brick and speklagen, three window columns with segmental heads.",
    "walls[3] Van Eeghenstraat veranda fronts (panels 181, 15, 75; crops w07-160/w08-160 2023-01-10): three decks of white timber verandas, round arches on slender posts with turned balustrades, across the whole front (new `gallery` component).",
    "INFERRED: the courtyard and party walls (otherWalls, brick grid at the civic pitch).",
    "budgetTriangles 21000: a 71 m, five-storey block on three street fronts with two veranda stacks (galleries) and speklagen; the 12k default cannot hold its storey and bay count. HOLD: the PDOK LoD2.2 shell (3DBAG API timed out) leaves a 2.3 m wall (surface 152) standing ground-to-roof inside the Van Eeghenstraat wing with no side walls under the 20.4 m roof: 40.8 m of vertical open edge that shellRepair cannot close (its seam rule pairs edges <= 0.6 m apart). Install after a 3DBAG refetch or a repair rule for walls under a flat roof."
  ],
  "shellRepair": true,
  "budgetTriangles": 21000
}
